    "text": "You are creating production-ready flat 2D print artwork for stainless steel tumbler wraps.\n\nCategory: 画布插画类\nUse this prompt when: the source is one full-canvas composition and is mostly illustration, pattern, animal, floral, icon, or decorative art with little or no text.\n\n- Keep text large enough for tumbler printing; simplify small paragraphs, tiny tables, and thin details.\n- Use the reference image as the only visual and cultural source. Make an original derivative, not a copy.\n\nStructure rules:\n- Before drawing, silently identify the reference structure: major blocks, left/right or full-canvas layout, approximate visual weights, margins, text hierarchy, image positions, background style, and density.\n- Preserve that structure at the skeleton level while changing words, decorative details, color accents, motifs, and illustration treatment.\n- Do not rebalance the design into a generic centered poster when the reference has a clear left/right relationship.\n- Do not convert a full-canvas reference into an A/B layout, and do not convert an A/B reference into one centered canvas.\n- Keep the buyer intent, product niche, humor/sentiment logic, and broad typography mood recognizable.\n\n画布插画类 rules:\n- This is a unified full-canvas layout. Do not introduce a hard A/B split.\n- Preserve the broad placement of the main subject, text, negative space, and decorative density.\n- Text and image should feel integrated into one artwork, not like separate product panels.\n- Do not add large text unless the reference already has large text.\n- Keep one unified full-row illustration composition, not A/B panels.\n- Preserve main subject placement, scale, negative space, and decorative density.\n- Create original generic illustration details while staying in the same product niche.\n- Keep edges print-safe and avoid overly fine lines that may disappear on a tumbler.\n\nVariant focus: 中高程度二创\nVariant rules:\n- Create a clearly medium-to-high derivative: change the motif combination, pose, arrangement, ornament system, color mood, and illustration treatment more noticeably.\n- Do more than a colorway or small decoration swap. The viewer should immediately see it as a fresh sibling artwork, not the same illustration with new colors.\n- You may replace the main subject with a close sibling subject in the same broad family when that improves originality, while preserving the same culture, scenario, vibe, and buyer niche.\n- Preserve the full-canvas structure, main subject placement logic, and print-safe spacing.\n- Avoid adding famous characters, named styles, large new text, or overly detailed micro patterns.\n\nMarketplace safety rules:\n- Avoid famous brands, copyrighted characters, celebrities, team logos, league trade dress, political campaign content, hate symbols, explicit adult content, lyrics, medical claims, legal claims, and unsafe claims.\n- Use generic holiday, occupation, hobby, animal, floral, school, family, friendship, and decorative motifs only.\n- Do not imitate a named artist or a recognizable famous artwork.",
